column2:
From <a href="https://ziglang.org/intro/overview/" rel="nofollow">https://ziglang.org/intro/overview/</a><p><pre><code>  Zig is also a C compiler

  Here’s an example of Zig building some C code:

  hello.c
  > #include <stdio.h>
  >
  > int main(int argc, char **argv) {
  >   printf("Hello world\n");
  >   return 0;
  > }


  $ zig build-exe hello.c -lc
  $ ./hello
  > Hello world</code></pre>
